From: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Stations: register the authored approach channel on the
 corridor bearing; wide structures get a local-roof clearance grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

place_station_trade_hub's open flight lane is authored at ~250deg while each station stamps its own corridor bearing (Helios 135deg) — the whole dock approach ran under solid roof, and the whole-city AABB pinned the chase camera at ~377 WU so the hull was roof-occluded on every approach (11/25 sampled frames, berth ceiling 125 WU).

Rotate the authored visual root about its visual center so the package's measured open channel lands on the station's effective corridor bearing (AUTHORED_APPROACH_CHANNEL_DEG per placeFile; proxy, berth and routing untouched). Then fix the ratchet the registration exposed: for roots wider than 240 WU, cameraClearanceFloorAt now reads a per-column occupancy grid rasterized from real triangles once per authored commit instead of one city-spanning AABB — the floor tracks the roof actually under the camera.

Witness: new scripts/probe-station-occlusion.mjs (SF_OCCL_MAP=1 polar roof map + bearing shots; approach leg waits for authored commit). After: 1/50 occluded samples on the authored leg, berth ceiling 50 WU, camY rides 110-215 over local roofs instead of pinned at 377.
Co-Authored-By: Robin Gattis <93robingattis@gmail.com>
